role:bpa a org:Role ;
    dcterms:source src:downstream-process-map ;
    skos:altLabel "BP&A"@en ;
    skos:definition "A team that captures, analyzes, forecasts and reports financial and operational data in support of a commercial organization."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "BP&A expanded as Business Planning and Analysis (Hamid, 2026-10-18 (EPM-DEC-001-0045)). externally corroborated: MPC job postings read \"The Business Planning and Analysis (BP&A) team is responsible for capturing, analyzing, forecasting, and reporting financial and operational data in support of the …\" and name the organization served, such as \"the Specialty Products (including Asphalt, Petrochemicals, and Petroleum Coke/Sulfur) commercial organization\" (MPC postings 00023257 and 00024586, read through a search index and third-party hosts, 2026-10-19). The definition is Claude's, adapted from that sentence. Whether the RACI entry means the team or one position is not settled; kept as a team."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Business Planning and Analysis"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "The source names a team here, not a position. The role stands for the team acting as one party in a RACI chart."@en .

